**AWS Instance Pricing Options:**
1. Ondemand Instance:
--> Pay for what you use:
----> Linux or Windows: billing per second, 70 sec -> 1 min 10 sec 
----> All other OS : billing per hour
--> has the highest cost but no upfront payment
--> no long term commitment
--> Recommended for short term workload.

2. Reserved Instance:
--> up to 72% discount compared to ondemand instance
--> Reservation period: 1 year or 3 years 
--> Payment options: No upfront, partial upfront, full upfront

3. Spot instance:
--> upto 90% discount compared to on demand
--> unused capacity
--> the MOST cost efficient instance in AWS
--> Not suitable for critical jobs or database
--> suitable for testing, batch processing, data analysis 

4. Dedicated Host:
--> A physical server with EC2 instance capacity fully dedicated to your use.
--> the Most expensive option

5. EC2 saving plans:
--> 72% discount
--> commit to a certain type of usage ( $10/hour for 1 year or 3 years)

6. Capacity Reservation:
--> reserve on demand instance capacity in a specific AZ for any duration
--> you always have access to EC2 capacity when you need it.
--> no time commitment, no billing discount
--> you are charged at on demand rate whether you run instance or Not

